python
boot seed 20261117 clock 1763400000 updates area
rng 51909 3b8e3587
step 1 "@connect b"
rng 51909 3b8e3587
step 2 "Planner"
out b "\n\r\n\rTHIS IS A MUD BASED ON.....\n\r\n\r                                ROM Version 2.4 beta\n\r\n\r               Original DikuMUD by Hans Staerfeldt, Katja Nyboe,\n\r               Tom Madsen, Michael Seifert, and Sebastian Hammer\n\r               Based on MERC 2.1 code by Hatchet, Furey, and Kahn\n\r               ROM 2.4 copyright (c) 1993-1998 Russ Taylor\n\r\n\rBy what name do you wish to be known? Password: \xff\xfb\x01"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 3 "smoke123"
out b "\n\r\xff\xfc\x01Welcome Immortal!\n\r\n\rYou are responsible for following the laws of immortal behavior. These can\n\rbe found by typing 'help laws' or 'help commandments'.\n\r\n\r* Excessive loading is not allowed, and is grounds for deletion.\n\r\n\r* Asking for promotion is grounds for instant deletion.\n\r\n\r* Type 'help jobs' to get some idea of what you should be doing.\n\r\n\r [Hit Return to continue]\n\r"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 4 "@return"
out b "\n\r* You are responsible for knowing the rules (type 'rules').  Ignorance of \n\r  the rules is no excuse.\n\r* Important commands: help, commands, news, notes\n\r* Use the delete command to erase unwanted characters\n\r  \n\r[Hit Return to continue]\n\r"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 5 "@return"
out b "\n\rWelcome to QuickMUD-Python.  Please don't feed the mobiles!\n\rThe Temple Of Mota [Room 3001]\n\r  You are in the southern end of the temple hall in the Temple of Mota.\n\rThe temple has been constructed from giant marble blocks, eternal in\n\rappearance, and most of the walls are covered by ancient wall paintings\n\rpicturing gods, giants and peasants.\n\r   Large steps lead down through the grand temple gate, descending the huge\n\rmound upon which the temple is built and ends on the temple square below.\n\r   Equally large steps lead UP through a small door into the ENTRANCE to MUD \n\rSCHOOL.  (type 'up' to go to MUD SCHOOL.)  A small plaque is on this wall.\n\rHassan is here, waiting to dispense some justice.\n\r\nNum          Name Unread Description\n\r==== ============ ====== =============================\n\r( 1)      General [   0] General discussion\n\r( 2)        Ideas [   0] Suggestion for improvement\n\r( 3)     Announce [   0] Announcements from Immortals\n\r( 4)         Bugs [   0] Typos, bugs, errors\n\r( 5)     Personal [   0] Personal messages\n\r\n\rYou current board is General.\n\rYou can both read and write on this board.\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 6 "scroll 0"
out b "Paging disabled.\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 7 "goto 3001"
out b "The Temple Of Mota [Room 3001]\n\r  You are in the southern end of the temple hall in the Temple of Mota.\n\rThe temple has been constructed from giant marble blocks, eternal in\n\rappearance, and most of the walls are covered by ancient wall paintings\n\rpicturing gods, giants and peasants.\n\r   Large steps lead down through the grand temple gate, descending the huge\n\rmound upon which the temple is built and ends on the temple square below.\n\r   Equally large steps lead UP through a small door into the ENTRANCE to MUD \n\rSCHOOL.  (type 'up' to go to MUD SCHOOL.)  A small plaque is on this wall.\n\rHassan is here, waiting to dispense some justice.\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 8 "hedit"
out b "HEdit:  There is no default help to edit.\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 9 "hedit nonsuch"
out b "HEdit:  There is no default help to edit.\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 10 "hedit new"
out b "\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 11 "edit help qmconfig"
out b "Syntax: EDIT AREA [create/reset] [vnum]     - Area Creation and Repoping.\n\rSyntax: EDIT ROOM ( [create] [vnum] )       - Room Creation and Editing.\n\rSyntax: EDIT OBJ  [create] <vnum>           - Object Creation and Editing.\n\rSyntax: EDIT MOB  [create] <vnum>           - Mobile Creation and Editing.\n\rSyntax: EDIT MP   [create] <vnum>           - MobProg Creation/Editing.\n\r\n\rSyntax: ASAVE  <world/area/changed/list>    - Save Editing to Disk.\n\rSyntax: ALIST                               - Listing of Areas.\n\rSyntax: RESET  See Help Resets.             - Set Game Resets.\n\r\n\rDefinition: [optional]  <required>  (combined arguments)\n\r\n\r     The above commands are used to expand the game world.  The original\n\rcode is based on was written by Surreality and installed in The Isles by Locke.\n\rIt was then converted to work with Envy by Jason Dinkel, and ported to ROM\n\r2.3 by Hans Birkeland (Hugin). Port to Rom 2.4 by Ivan Toledo (ver 1.7).\n\r\n\r     Inside an editor, typing COMMANDS lists working commands and ? gives\n\rhelp. AEDIT and REDIT default to the current area or room. EDIT ROOM RESET\n\rresets the current room.  Most commands with no arguments display syntax.\n\rSee also help: AEDIT REDIT MEDIT OEDIT\n\r\n\r============================================================\n\r\n\rOLCSAVE\n\rA help in an area file, which asave writes back with the area.\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 12 "edit hedit qmconfig"
out b "\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 13 "@return"
out b "Keyword : [QMCONFIG]\n\rLevel   : [0]\n\rText    :\n\rSyntax: qmconfig [show|ansiprompt|ansicolor|telnetga] [on|off]\n\r\n\r        This command is used to set options developed in the\n\r        QuickMUD source. They include:\n\r\n\r        ansicolor  - do new logins have color on by default?\n\r        ansiprompt - do new logins see a \"color?\" prompt?\n\r        show       - show current settings of qmconfig variables\n\r        telnetga   - do new logins have telnetga enabled?\n\r-END-\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 14 "show"
out b "Keyword : [QMCONFIG]\n\rLevel   : [0]\n\rText    :\n\rSyntax: qmconfig [show|ansiprompt|ansicolor|telnetga] [on|off]\n\r\n\r        This command is used to set options developed in the\n\r        QuickMUD source. They include:\n\r\n\r        ansicolor  - do new logins have color on by default?\n\r        ansiprompt - do new logins see a \"color?\" prompt?\n\r        show       - show current settings of qmconfig variables\n\r        telnetga   - do new logins have telnetga enabled?\n\r-END-\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 15 "commands"
out b "keyword        text           new            level          commands       \n\rdelete         list           show           ?              \n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 16 "?"
out b "Syntax:  ? [command]\n\r\n\r[command]  [description]\n\rArea       -Area attributes.\n\rRoom       -Room attributes.\n\rSector     -Sector types, terrain.\n\rExit       -Exit types.\n\rType       -Types of objects.\n\rExtra      -Object attributes.\n\rWear       -Where to wear object.\n\rSpec       -Available special programs.\n\rSex        -Sexes.\n\rAct        -Mobile attributes.\n\rAffect     -Mobile affects.\n\rWear-loc   -Where mobile wears object.\n\rSpells     -Names of current spells.\n\rContainer  -Container status.\n\rArmor      -Ac for different attacks.\n\rApply      -Apply flags\n\rForm       -Mobile body form.\n\rPart       -Mobile body parts.\n\rImm        -Mobile immunity.\n\rRes        -Mobile resistance.\n\rVuln       -Mobile vulnerability.\n\rOff        -Mobile offensive behaviour.\n\rSize       -Mobile size.\n\rPosition   -Mobile positions.\n\rWclass     -Weapon class.\n\rWtype      -Special weapon type.\n\rPortal     -Portal types.\n\rFurniture  -Furniture types.\n\rLiquid     -Liquid types.\n\rApptype    -Apply types.\n\rWeapon     -Weapon types.\n\rMprog      -MobProgram flags.\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 17 "xyzzy"
out b "Huh?\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 18 "keyword"
out b "Syntax: keyword [keywords]\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
rng 51929 534cb46e
step 19 "keyword QMCONFIG QM"
out b "Ok.\n\r\n\r<100hp 100m 100mv> \xff\xf9"
